            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Viburnum propinquum, the Chinese evergreen viburnum, is a species of flowering plant in the family Viburnaceae, native to central and southern China, Taiwan, and Luzon in the Philippines. A dense, rounded evergreen bush reaching {{cvt|6|–|8|ft}}, and useful for landscaping applications, it is hardy to USDA zone 7."
